# File: tests/features/routed-turns.feature
# Generated from: specs/3-answer-routed-model-turns-through-provider-adapters-with-streaming-tools-thinking-and-clear-errors/requirements.md
Feature: Routed-model turns through provider adapters

  @SCN001
  Scenario: Claude steps pass through untouched
    Given a step whose model is "claude-haiku-5-5"
    When turn.step fires
    Then the hook yields next(e) unchanged with no HTTP request, subprocess or credential read

  @SCN002
  Scenario: A routed model completes an agentic turn
    Given a step for "opencode-go/kimi-k3.1-pro" with a stored credential and responses that call Read, then Edit, then answer
    When each step fires
    Then each request carries the captured system prompt, the session conversation and the offered tools, and the turn ends with the model's final text without calling next

  @SCN003
  Scenario: Every wire format maps to the same chunks
    Given Chat Completions, Responses, Codex and Anthropic Messages streams
    When each is translated
    Then text, tool calls, reasoning, stop reason and usage map to the same engine chunks

  @SCN004
  Scenario: Switching models keeps context
    Given a session that answered on a Claude model
    When the user switches to a routed model and back
    Then the routed request contains the Claude turns and the next Claude step passes through

  @SCN005
  Scenario: Guards and identity apply to every routed request
    Given a routed OpenCode Go step
    When it is sent and answered
    Then the request and response guards run, the request goes only to the provider host, and it carries the session's x-opencode-session id and "nmg-router/<version>" user agent

  @SCN006
  Scenario: Only offered tools are sent with generated schemas
    Given the generated built-in tool schema registry and a step offering Read, Edit and an MCP tool
    When the request is built
    Then Read and Edit are sent with their schemas, the MCP tool is left out and named in a debug log, and a stale registry fails its test

  @SCN007
  Scenario: Responses stream through curl with secrets on stdin
    Given a fake curl child that emits SSE pieces
    When a routed step runs
    Then text chunks arrive before the child ends, tool calls arrive once complete, secrets appear only on stdin, an interrupt stops the child, and speed metrics are recorded

  @SCN008
  Scenario: Thinking effort is clamped per model
    Given a model supporting only low and medium
    When a step arrives with effort max
    Then the request carries effort medium and the status line shows the model id and "thinking medium"

  @SCN009
  Scenario: Failures end with a clear message and no fallback
    Given a routed step that gets a 429 with retry-after
    When it runs
    Then it ends with a rate-limit message naming the provider and the wait, the status line shows the error, and next is never called
